# Accessibility Rules

All Geordi UI must meet WCAG 2.2 AA minimum.

## HTML

- Use semantic elements: `button`, `fieldset`, `legend`, `label`, `select`, `main`, `section`
- Never use `<div onclick>` for interactive controls
- Every form control has an associated `<label>`

## ARIA

- Status updates use `role="status"` with `aria-live="polite"`
- Decorative elements use `aria-hidden="true"` or `.visually-hidden` class
- Section headings use `aria-labelledby` on `<section>`

## Keyboard

- All controls reachable via Tab
- `:focus-visible` outline on every interactive element (3px, high contrast)
- No keyboard traps

## Visual

- WCAG 2.2 AA contrast ratio (4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for large text)
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`
- Respect `prefers-color-scheme: dark`

## Testing

Manual checklist in `docs/TESTING.md`. Any UI PR must pass keyboard-only navigation.
